# Install CVAT-part

After Docker 26.0 installation, install nuclio and deploy CVAT-part

[comment]:#################################################################
`nuclio` installation
```sh
sudo curl -sSL \
  "https://github.com/nuclio/nuclio/releases/download/1.15.9/nuctl-1.15.9-linux-amd64" \
  -o /usr/local/bin/nuctl

sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/nuctl
nuctl version
```

[comment]:#################################################################
Create an admin user for CVAT:
```sh
docker exec -it cvat_server bash -ic \
  "python manage.py createsuperuser"
```

[comment]:#################################################################
Start CVAT with the serverless stack:
```sh
docker network create cvat 2>/dev/null || true

docker compose \
  -f docker-compose.yml \
  -f components/serverless/docker-compose.serverless.yml \
  up -d
```


[comment]:#################################################################
Create nuctl project and deploy it:
```sh
nuctl create project cvat --platform local
nuctl get projects --platform local

nuctl deploy \
  --project-name cvat \
  --path serverless/pytorch/facebookresearch/sam/nuclio \
  --platform local

nuctl get functions --platform local
```

Finally, you can connect to http://localhost:8080 and enjoy the annotation task ;D

Once you have finished all your annotation activiteies, you can stop all the containers
```sh
docker stop $(docker ps -a -q)
```


and remove all of them
```sh
docker rm $(docker ps -a -q)
```
